<title>UK: European cotton business slow.</title>
<headline>European cotton business slow.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in raw cotton remained generally slow as the holiday influences increased in several countries, traders said.</p>
<p>But the principal factors restricting demand have been the lack of fresh price stimulus and, in some cases, the adverse movement of currency exchange values.</p>
<p>Poland continued to indicate that growths other than Central Asian may attract increased attention during the next few months.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
